---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const services = [
  {
    kicker: "Flow cytometry & spectral",
    title: "Panels that work the first time",
    body: "Multicolor and full spectral panel design, unmixing and controls strategy, instrument QC, and the troubleshooting that gets a stalled experiment moving again. Fifteen years on conventional and spectral platforms, and a granted patent on modeling and minimizing spillover spreading.",
    points: [
      "Panel design and spillover-spread review",
      "Spectral setup, unmixing, and control strategy",
      "Core facility operations, rates, and QC programs",
      "Training for teams new to spectral",
    ],
  },
  {
    kicker: "Product strategy",
    title: "Requirements from the bench, not the boardroom",
    body: "Fractional product leadership for instrument and software companies selling into life science. Requirements gathered face to face with the scientists who use the thing, then the business cases, pricing, and roadmaps that survive contact with reality.",
    points: [
      "Voice-of-customer and user research programs",
      "Business cases, ROI models, and pricing structure",
      "Roadmap and release planning across scrum teams",
      "Competitive and market assessment",
    ],
  },
  {
    kicker: "Cell therapy automation",
    title: "Closing the loop on manufacturing",
    body: "Advisory on automated cell therapy manufacturing: how analytics and sorting integrate into a closed process, and what traceability a platform needs before it can make real patient doses under FDA-regulated quality systems.",
    points: [
      "In-process and release analytics integration",
      "Closed-system cell selection and sorting",
      "Traceability, records, and quality-system readiness",
      "Technical due diligence for investors and partners",
    ],
  },
];

const engagements = [
  {
    title: "Start with a call",
    body: "Thirty minutes, no charge, to find out whether the problem is one I can actually help with. If it is not, I will usually know who can.",
  },
  {
    title: "Scope the work",
    body: "A short written proposal: the question, what you get, and what it costs. Half-day advisory sessions, fixed-scope projects, and monthly fractional retainers all work.",
  },
  {
    title: "Do the work",
    body: "On your instruments, in your data, or alongside your product team. You get artifacts you can use without me: panel files, protocols, requirement docs, business cases.",
  },
];

const schema = [
  {
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "@id": "https://thisishowwesee.com/#webpage",
    url: "https://thisishowwesee.com/",
    name: "How We See LLC — flow cytometry and cell therapy consulting",
    about: { "@id": "https://thisishowwesee.com/#business" },
  },
  {
    "@type": "OfferCatalog",
    name: "Consulting services",
    itemListElement: services.map((service) => ({
      "@type": "Offer",
      itemOffered: {
        "@type": "Service",
        name: service.kicker,
        description: service.body,
        provider: { "@id": "https://thisishowwesee.com/#business" },
      },
    })),
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="How We See LLC — Flow Cytometry & Cell Therapy Consulting | Howie Seay"
  description="How We See LLC is Howie Seay's consulting practice: flow cytometry and spectral panel design, product strategy for life-science tools, and cell therapy manufacturing automation."
  schema={schema}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">How We See LLC</p>
      <h1>Flow cytometry consulting, <span class="accent">bench to product</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">
        Good data is still harder to get than it should be. I am Howie Seay, an innovative product
        leader and board-certified cytometrist, and How We See LLC is where I help labs, core
        facilities, and instrument makers close the gap: panel design and spectral analysis,
        product strategy for life-science tools, and automated cell therapy manufacturing.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a href="mailto:howie@thisishowwesee.com" class="button special">Start a conversation</a>
        <a href="/about" class="button">About Howie</a>
      </div>

      <div class="stats">
        <div>
          <span class="stat-num">15+</span>
          <span class="stat-label">Years in cytometry</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="stat-num">2</span>
          <span class="stat-label">Granted patents</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="stat-num">15+</span>
          <span class="stat-label">Publications</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="stat-num">SCYM</span>
          <span class="stat-label">Board certified (ASCP)</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">01 / Services</p>
      <h2>What How We See does</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--text-dim); margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
        Three threads, one idea: measurement you can trust, at the scale medicine needs.
      </p>

      <div class="feature-grid">
        {
          services.map((service) => (
            <article class="feature-card">
              <p class="feature-kicker">{service.kicker}</p>
              <h3>{service.title}</h3>
              <p>{service.body}</p>
              <ul>
                {service.points.map((point) => (
                  <li>{point}</li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">02 / Engagements</p>
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        {
          engagements.map((step) => (
            <li>
              <h3>{step.title}</h3>
              <p>{step.body}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">03 / Credentials</p>
          <h2>Why me</h2>
          <p>
            I ran fee-for-service cytometry and sorting cores at the University of Florida, invented
            and patented a panel design method at BD, helped build the spectral unmixing in FlowJo,
            and now lead product for an automated cell therapy manufacturing platform. The receipts
            are public.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a href="/cv" class="button">View CV</a>
            <a href="/pubs" class="button">Publications</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="split-media">
          <img src="/images/pic01.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">04 / Resources</p>
      <h2>Free, before you hire anyone</h2>
      <p>
        A curated guide to flow cytometry: the communities worth joining, the books worth reading,
        the software worth learning, and the courses worth the time. Everything I wish someone had
        handed me on day one. There is also a compensation guide, so you know what this work is
        worth on either side of the table.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a href="/flowsites" class="button">Browse the resources</a>
        <a href="/compensation" class="button">Compensation guide</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">05 / Contact</p>
      <h2>Let's talk</h2>
      <p>
        Tell me what you are measuring and what is going wrong. Email is the fastest way to reach
        How We See LLC; LinkedIn works too.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a href="mailto:howie@thisishowwesee.com" class="button special"
          >howie@thisishowwesee.com</a
        >
        <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/this-is-how-we-see/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="button">Connect on LinkedIn</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
